---
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-8">
  <SectionHeader
    badge="PDF OCR GUIDE"
    title="Everything You Need to Know About"
    highlight="PDF to Text"
    suffix="Conversion"
    description="Learn how PDF OCR works, when you need it, and how Hayvex converts scanned PDF documents into editable text securely inside your browser."
  />

  <div class="prose prose-invert prose-zinc mx-auto mt-14 max-w-none">

    <h2>What is PDF to Text?</h2>

    <p>
      PDF to Text is the process of extracting readable and editable text from a
      PDF document. While many PDFs already contain selectable text, scanned
      PDFs are simply collections of images. OCR (Optical Character Recognition)
      analyzes those images and converts the visible characters into editable
      digital text.
    </p>

    <p>
      Hayvex performs this conversion directly inside your browser, allowing you
      to extract text without uploading sensitive documents to external servers.
      This browser-based approach provides both speed and privacy for personal
      and professional documents.
    </p>

    <h2>How PDF OCR Works</h2>

    <p>
      OCR technology examines each page of a scanned PDF, identifies letters,
      numbers and symbols, and reconstructs them as machine-readable text.
      Modern OCR engines use pattern recognition and machine learning to improve
      recognition accuracy even when documents contain different fonts, layouts
      or varying image quality.
    </p>

    <p>
      Hayvex processes every page efficiently while preserving document privacy,
      making it suitable for reports, contracts, study material and archived
      paperwork.
    </p>

    <h2>Why Convert PDFs to Text?</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Edit scanned documents without retyping everything.</li>
      <li>Search text inside previously scanned PDFs.</li>
      <li>Reuse content in reports and presentations.</li>
      <li>Digitize printed archives.</li>
      <li>Improve accessibility of scanned documents.</li>
      <li>Save hours of manual data entry.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Common Use Cases</h2>

    <p>
      Students use PDF OCR to convert printed notes into editable study
      material. Businesses extract information from invoices, contracts and
      reports. Researchers digitize historical documents, while professionals
      convert scanned forms and records into searchable digital files.
    </p>

    <h2>Tips for Better OCR Accuracy</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Use high-quality scanned PDFs whenever possible.</li>
      <li>Avoid blurry or heavily compressed documents.</li>
      <li>Ensure pages are properly aligned.</li>
      <li>Scan documents at 300 DPI or higher for best results.</li>
      <li>Keep text unobstructed by marks or folds.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Supported PDF Documents</h2>

    <p>
      Hayvex works well with scanned documents, printed reports, invoices,
      receipts, books, forms and image-based PDFs. Native PDFs that already
      contain selectable text may not require OCR, but scanned PDFs benefit
      significantly from OCR processing.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy First PDF OCR</h2>

    <p>
      Many online PDF converters require documents to be uploaded before
      processing begins. Hayvex follows a privacy-first approach by performing
      OCR locally in your browser whenever possible. Your documents stay under
      your control throughout the conversion process.
    </p>

    <h2>Why Choose Hayvex?</h2>

    <p>
      Hayvex is built to deliver fast, accurate and secure PDF OCR with a clean,
      browser-based experience. Whether you need to extract text from scanned
      reports, books, invoices or forms, Hayvex helps you work more efficiently
      while protecting your privacy. Future updates will expand support for
      document intelligence features including table extraction, document
      comparison and AI-powered document analysis.
    </p>

  </div>
</section>